<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's Matav Rt boosts profits in 1996.</title>
<headline>Hungary's Matav Rt boosts profits in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>				     Jan-Dec 1996   Jan-Dec 1995</p>
<p>    Group operating profit     37,518.9  vs   29,597.8</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit	 23,800.9  vs    3,194.1</p>
<p>    Group after-tax profit     23,560.9  vs    3,099.9</p>
<p>    Group net sales	     192,418.3  vs  141,618.0</p>
<p>    Group other revenue	   6,282.9  vs    5,447.1</p>
<p>    Material expenditures	31,375.2  vs   27,395.1</p>
<p>    Personnel expenditures     35,183.1  vs   28,870.9</p>
<p>    Depreciation		   34,408.4  vs   26,223.7</p>
<p>    Other costs		    38,400.5  vs   31,685.5</p>
<p>    Other expenditures	   28,689.4  vs   29,597.8</p>
<p>    Net financial income	 11,445.1 loss vs 9,018.1 loss</p>
<p>    Net extraordinary income    2,272.8 loss vs 2,078.6</p>
<p>    Taxation			    240.0  vs	 94.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Matav is a telecommunications company, it is 67 percent owned by a 50-50 consortium of Deutsche Telekom and Ameritech. The figures are consolidated.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
